<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Darya-i-Noor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Darya-i-Noor ('Sea of Light') is a large pale pink diamond, among the most famous gems in the world. It was taken from the Mughal treasury in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>, along with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koh-i-noor">Koh-i-Noor</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peacock-throne">Peacock Throne</a>, and carried back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. It remains among the Iranian crown jewels.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/darya-i-noor.jpg" alt="Darya-i-Noor" width="294" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Daria-e_Noor_(Sea_of_Light)_Diamond_from_the_collection_of_the_national_jewels_of_Iran_at_Central_Bank_of_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
